# chat: `hi` is a greeting — one Jev (mock) intake request, a [you] bubble, a [jevcode] catalogue reply, no run, the badge
# stays the default (jev+llm); the wall time Enter → [jevcode] is read from the timing file (TUI-DESIGN-2 §3.1 row 6, §8.2 chat-hi)
expect \x1b\[\?25l
expect Say hi
expect sess \$
sleep 0.2
send hi
sleep 0.2
send \r
mark hi-sent
expect \[you\](?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* (?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)*hi
expect \[jevcode\](?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* Hi\.
mark hi-reply
expect jev\+llm
send /exit
sleep 0.2
send \r
eof
